WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
Here's a snowflake drawn by a maths rule, not the weather.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.850
Start with a triangle.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:12.230
Cut each edge into three equal pieces, take the middle piece out, and build a point in its place.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.450
Do that to every edge, again and again.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.230
This drawing is one stage along the way.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:24.410
The shape the rule is aiming at has an infinite perimeter: an edge longer than any ruler.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.270
How can a shape have an infinite perimeter?

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:34.210
In this mission, you'll measure round a plain triangle, then apply the rule once and see what it does to the path.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.410
You'll follow the rule stage by stage, keeping track of the edges.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.530
Your mission: explain how a shape can have an infinite perimeter.
